    [BugFix][Attention] Backport MLA layerwise KV load waits to v0.32 (#20477)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport #19639 to `releases/v0.32.0rc`. Short prefills can be
    classified as decode while still loading external KV. MLA now consumes
    the connector's layer load completion on all three preprocessing paths,
    and ordinary decode records the attention-compute boundary so subsequent
    layer prefetches can advance.
    
    The five-file change cherry-picks cleanly from the main PR. This
    backport does not change request classification or graph-mode
    configuration.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. It prevents incorrect output or an engine failure when an MLA short
    prefill reloads external KV through a layerwise connector. The release
    note fragment will be renamed to this PR's number after creation.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - On this v0.32.0rc base: Ruff check and format check passed for all
    four changed Python files; `py_compile` and `git diff --check` passed.
    - Local CPU pytest could not start: the available Python environment
    lacks `torch`. CI and v0.32 hardware validation remain pending.
    - Source PR #19639 documents CPU and NPU evidence on earlier branches.
    Those results are supporting evidence, not a claim that this backport
    passed v0.32 NPU validation.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] Regression tests and boundary cases are included from #19639.
    - [ ] CPU tests passed on the v0.32 branch.
    - [ ] v0.32 NPU validation completed.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
